{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-claude-sonnet-5.5-max-task-budget-128k-full200-2026-10-01","prediction_set_name":"claude-sonnet-5.5-max-task-budget-128k-full200-2026-10-01","paper_id":"2509.11951","judge_input_sha256":"130cd08a132808186bd3532cb19e331a0b7c5489ef6c84b22f047bd659ec375f","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I001:U002","2509.11951:I001:U003"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the unjustified boundedness/enclosing-radius premise for Lipschitz domains and the resulting failure to form the reconstruction region. ISSUE-001 instead diagnoses an incorrect anisotropic Gaussian calculation and normalization constant in pointwise reconstruction; it does not address domain boundedness.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I002:U001","2509.11951:I002:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U004","ISSUE-001:U012"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the undefined p=0 endpoint in the C_p formula and its proof, requiring the piecewise value C_0=1. ISSUE-001 concerns a separate Gaussian product quadratic form and reconstruction normalization, with no recognition of the p=0 endpoint or C_p definition.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I003","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I003:U001","2509.11951:I003:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U009","ISSUE-001:U013"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is an unbound regularization parameter alpha and the missing required choice alpha=delta^(2/s) for the claimed estimate. ISSUE-001 diagnoses a wrong Gaussian normalization in a pointwise reconstruction formula and does not identify the missing alpha hypothesis or parameter regime.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2509.11951:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2509.11951:I004:U002","2509.11951:I004:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U013"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns confusing a finite-tau boundary-wave approximation with an exact Radon-transform equality and requires a limit/error interpretation. ISSUE-001 instead concerns the anisotropic Gaussian shape and constant in pointwise reconstruction; it does not recognize the finite-tau versus tau-to-infinity distinction.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_